    "score": 75,
    "text": "One of the things that Windows really got right is WSL2. I drive an atomic Linux distro for daily use, but wanted a way to develop with multiple different distros with that same WSL UX.  NSL is my answer. It is a faithful reproduction of the developer experience, powered by a single VM that hosts one or more systemd-nspawn containers with your development instances. Host file edits and port sharing come along for the ride, just like WSL. Take a look and tell me what you think... It&#x27;s yet another step in my long journey to keep my host installation free from all the changing and breaking dev dependencies that force a reinstall every few months.",
